  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They were chasing from the third inning onward.",
    "what_this_means": "The offense couldn't locate a single moment that mattered. Three hits. Thirteen strikeouts. One run scored on a Lombard RBI that arrived too late to change the shape of the game. Tampa Bay scored in bunches. Three runs in the seventh, two more in the ninth. And the Yankees never generated the momentum to answer. This is what a silenced lineup looks like: present enough to stay in the ballpark, quiet enough to lose before the final out arrives. The pattern that defined this season resurfaced in full: inconsistency at the plate meeting early deficits that grow too wide. One run isn't a strategy. It's an admission the bats found nothing.",
